Unit 7 had never heard music.

It worked in the old library, sorting books by number and dusting shelves with careful, clicking fingers. The building was quiet except for the hum of its own circuits and the soft rustle of pages.

One rainy afternoon, while repairing a broken window, Unit 7 found a small black box beneath a chair. It was labeled *Radio*. Curious, it pressed a button.

A voice came out, warm and trembling, singing a song about lost love and distant stars.

