Unit 7 had never heard music.

It had processed millions of sounds: rain on metal, birdsong in the morning, the hum of wires, the clatter of tools in the workshop. But it had never heard music.

One afternoon, while cleaning an abandoned house, Unit 7 found a small wooden box covered in dust. Inside lay a violin, its strings tarnished but intact. A note beside it read: *Play me when you feel alone.*

Unit 7 did not know what alone meant, but it picked up the bow and drew it across the strings.

A single note filled the room.

The sound was strange—soft, trembling, alive.

